   "reply": "Step 1 is done. I added `src/ledgerlite/money.py` with `parse(value: str | Decimal) -> Decimal`. I haven't run or tested it.\n\n- **Types:** it raises `TypeError` for anything that isn't a `str` or `Decimal`, so floats and ints are rejected.\n- **Bad strings:** an unparseable string raises `ValueError`.\n- **Non-finite values:** `NaN` and `Infinity` raise `ValueError`.\n- **Non-positive values:** zero and negatives raise `ValueError(\"amount must be positive\")`. The message matches the one `Ledger.transfer` uses now.\n\n**Next step (2):** change `Ledger.transfer` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py` to call `money.parse(amount)` instead of `Decimal(amount)` plus the inline `<= 0` check. I'll stop here until you tell me to go ahead.\n\nTwo things to decide before step 2:\n- `transfer` currently raises `decimal.InvalidOperation` for a malformed string. After the change it will raise `ValueError`.\n- `transfer` is annotated `amount: str`. I'd widen it to `str | Decimal` to match `parse`.",
