   "reply": "I did one step: `Ledger.transfer` now calls `money.parse` instead of parsing the amount itself. I then ran the tests, and both pass.\n\nI had no record of where the refactor stopped, and the directory isn't a git repo. I inferred the step from the code. `money.py` already had a `parse` helper that nothing used, and `transfer` still had its own `Decimal` parsing. If you had a different next step in mind, tell me and I'll redo it.\n\nThe change is in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`:\n- I added `from . import money`.\n- I replaced the inline `Decimal(amount)` and the positive-amount check with `money.parse(amount)`.\n\n`transfer` now also rejects non-finite amounts like `NaN` and `Infinity`, and it rejects malformed strings with a clear `ValueError`. Before, those cases got a raw `InvalidOperation` or slipped through. No test covers those cases yet.\n\nMy first test run failed because I passed `-I`, which makes Python ignore `PYTHONPATH`. I reran without it.",
